1. Executive Summary & Product Vision
1.1 Mission
Eliminate the need for citizens to physically visit the municipality to report urban problems, while giving municipal leadership real-time visibility and complete traceability of every request — from submission to resolution.

1.2 Product Vision
FixMaCity is a web application that digitalizes the complete lifecycle of citizen requests for the Municipality of Sousse, Tunisia. It directly connects residents of the three délégations (Sousse Ville, Sousse Jawhara, Sousse Sidi Abdelhamid) with the relevant municipal services, eliminating traditional bureaucratic friction.

The platform is built around four distinct human roles — Citoyen, Agent, Chef de service, and Président Municipal — each with a dedicated, secure, role-adapted interface. A trilingual AI chatbot assists citizens throughout their interactions.

1.3 MVP Scope
Dimension	MVP Value
Municipalities	1 — Sousse
Délégations	3 — Sousse Ville · Sousse Jawhara · Sousse Sidi Abdelhamid
Municipal departments	8 — Voirie, Éclairage, Déchets, Espaces verts, Signalisation, Réseaux, Administratif, Suggestions
Human roles	4 — Citoyen · Agent · Chef de service · Président municipal
System actors	1 — Chatbot IA (trilingual citizen assistant)
In-app messaging	None — permanently removed
SMS notifications	None — email + in-app only
Payments	None — fully free public service
Authentication	Email + password (citizens: self-registration / staff: created by admin)
Citizen statuses	3 simplified statuses: EN ATTENTE · EN COURS · TERMINÉ
 
2. Problem & Context
2.1 Current Situation — What Is Not Working
The Municipality of Sousse currently manages citizen requests through unstructured channels: physical counter visits, phone calls, paper mail. This obsolete infrastructure generates six critical pain points:

Pain Point	Affects	Impact & Consequence
Citizens must physically travel to the town hall to report a problem	Citoyen	Very low reporting rate. Most urban problems are never reported.
No acknowledgement — citizens do not know if their request exists	Citoyen	Zero trust in the system.
Requests managed by phone or paper — frequent information loss	Agents / Chefs	Forgotten requests. No traceability, no accountability.
Leadership has no real-time visibility	Président	Impossible to manage performance, identify bottlenecks.
The loop never closes — citizens do not know if their problem is resolved	Citoyen	Chronic frustration, distrust toward the municipality, civic disengagement.
 
3. Roles & Actors
FixMaCity relies on five distinct actors. The four human roles each have an authenticated interface with strictly defined permissions. The chatbot is a system actor integrated into the Citoyen interface.

3.1 Role Overview
Role	Who?	Primary Objective	Language
Citoyen	Residents of 3 délégations of Sousse	Submit, track, vote, rate, interact with chatbot	AR / FR / EN
Agent	Field agent assigned to a département	Receive requests, intervene, prove resolution by photo	French
Chef de service	Département head (1 per département)	Accept/refuse requests, assign to agents, supervise progress	French
Président municipal	Single super-administrator of the platform	Assign requests, manage org structure, monitor KPIs	French
Chatbot IA	System actor — AI assistant on citizen side	Answer questions, guide submission, check status	AR / FR / EN

3.2 Detailed Role Specifications
3.2.1 Citoyen
Account creation: Public self-registration — email + password + first name + last name + home délégation.

Permissions — What the Citoyen CAN do:
•	Create an account by self-registration (email + password)
•	Submit a signalement with category, title, description, optional photo, mandatory GPS location
•	Edit their signalement only if statut = EN ATTENTE (before any assignment)
•	Delete their signalement only if statut = EN ATTENTE
•	Track the simplified status of their requests: EN ATTENTE · EN COURS · TERMINÉ
•	Access the interactive map (login required) and view all active signalements
•	Vote for/against propositions published by the Président municipal
•	Recommend an existing signalement instead of creating a duplicate
•	Rate the service from 1 to 5 stars + optional comment after resolution
•	Interact with the Chatbot IA at any time
•	Choose their interface language (AR / FR / EN) — persisted in the database

Restrictions — What the Citoyen CANNOT do:
•	See the internal processing flow (assignments, refusals, internal steps)
•	Edit or delete a signalement after assignment
•	Access the Agent, Chef de service, or Président interfaces
•	Vote more than once for the same proposition or the same signalement
•	Contact staff by messaging (feature permanently removed)

3.2.2 Agent
Account creation: Exclusively by the Président municipal. No self-registration. The Agent is assigned to a specific département at account creation.

Permissions — What the Agent CAN do:
•	See ALL requests assigned to their département/team (team visibility)
•	Accept a request personally → statut changes to EN COURS
•	Refuse a request with a mandatory documented reason → returns to Chef de service
•	Add internal comments (visible only to Chef de service and team members)
•	Upload one or more proof-of-intervention photos (JPG/PNG, max 10 MB)
•	Mark a request as TERMINÉE — BLOCKED if no photo has been uploaded

Restrictions:
•	Cannot close a request without uploading at least one proof photo
•	Cannot see requests from other départements
•	Cannot assign or reassign requests

3.2.3 Chef de service
Structure: 1 Chef de service per département. Account created by the Président. A Chef can only supervise agents from their own département.

Permissions — What the Chef de service CAN do:
•	See all requests assigned to their département by the Président
•	Accept a request and assign it to an agent or team in their département
•	Refuse a request with documented reason → automatic return to Président
•	Monitor in real time the progress of all département requests
•	Add/deactivate (soft delete only) agents from their team
•	See each agent's workload (number of active requests)
•	Modify their département configuration (name, description, associated categories)
•	Access the département statistics dashboard
•	Export département data to CSV

Restrictions:
•	Cannot physically delete an agent — deactivation (soft delete) only
•	Cannot assign requests to agents from other départements
•	Cannot access global KPIs across all délégations

3.2.4 Président Municipal
Role: Single super-administrator of the platform. Full control over organizational structure, request routing, global KPIs, and publishing citizen proposals. There is only one active Président account at a time.

Permissions — What the Président CAN do:
•	View all incoming requests from all délégations and all départements
•	Manually assign each request to the relevant Chef de service
•	Directly assign a request to a département (alternative path)
•	Receive and reassign requests refused by Chefs (with reason for refusal)
•	Create, edit, deactivate Chef de service accounts (1 per département)
•	Create, edit, deactivate Agent accounts (assign each agent to a département)
•	Manage département structure: add, edit, configure categories
•	Publish municipal propositions for citizen voting
•	Access global KPI dashboard (all délégations, all départements)
•	Export performance reports (CSV / PDF)

3.2.5 Chatbot IA (System Actor — MVP)
The Chatbot appears as a full actor in the use case diagram. It is integrated in MVP as a trilingual citizen assistant.

What the Chatbot DOES:
•	Answer frequently asked questions about the platform
•	Guide the Citoyen step by step through submitting a signalement
•	Look up and communicate the status of the logged-in user's signalements
•	Detect the active session language and respond in the same language (AR / FR / EN)
•	Redirect to the correct feature or section of the application
•	Activate a fallback message if the question is outside its scope

Technical implementation:
•	LLM API: Gemini API — calls made exclusively server-side (Node.js backend)
•	LLM API key stored in environment variable — never exposed to the client
•	Strict trilingual system prompt defining scope, tone, and chatbot limits
•	Rate limiting on route /api/chatbot (20 req/min per user)
 
4. Categories & Départements
4.1 Definitions
Concept	Definition
Category	Type of problem reported by the Citoyen. A category can be handled by one or more départements. Example: 'Nid-de-poule' belongs to the Voirie category.
Département	Municipal service responsible for handling one or more problem categories. Each département is led by a single Chef de service. Example: Département Voirie & Routes.
Relation	A category can belong to multiple départements (N:N relation). The Président manually assigns each request to the relevant département, even when multiple départements share a category.

4.2 Départements of the Municipality of Sousse
#	Département (FR)	Département (AR)	Département (EN)	Category examples
1	Voirie & Routes	الطرق والأرصفة	Roads & Pavements	Nid-de-poule, trottoir dégradé, affaissement
2	Éclairage public	الإنارة العمومية	Street Lighting	Lampadaire cassé, câble exposé, zone non éclairée
3	Propreté & Déchets	النظافة والنفايات	Waste & Cleanliness	Dépôt sauvage, bac débordant, encombrant
4	Espaces verts	المساحات الخضراء	Green Spaces	Arbre dangereux, banc cassé, aire de jeux
5	Signalisation routière	الإشارات المرورية	Traffic Signaling	Feu défectueux, panneau manquant, marquage effacé
6	Réseaux & Drainage	الشبكات	Networks & Drainage	Fuite d'eau, drain bouché, inondation, regard cassé
7	Administratif	الشؤون الإدارية	Administrative	Permis en retard, documents municipaux, plaintes
8	Suggestions	الاقتراحات	Suggestions	Quality of life improvements, citizen proposals

Categories are fully configurable by the Président municipal. A Chef de service can modify the categories associated with their own département.
 
5. Request Lifecycle & Statuses
5.1 Citizen-Facing Statuses (Simplified — 3 States)
The Citoyen never sees the internal processing flow. They receive only three simplified statuses:

Citizen Status	Map Pin Color	Meaning
EN ATTENTE	Yellow	Signalement received. Under review or being internally processed (includes all internal statuses up to field intervention).
EN COURS	Blinking Blue	An Agent is actively intervening in the field.
TERMINÉ	Green	Problem resolved. Proof photo uploaded. Service rating invitation sent.

When a request is refused by a Chef de service or Agent and reassigned, the Citoyen continues to see EN ATTENTE. The internal refusal/reassignment flow is invisible to the Citoyen.

5.2 Internal Statuses (Municipal Staff)
Internal Status	Set By	Citizen Sees	Meaning
SOUMIS	System (auto)	EN ATTENTE	Signalement received — awaiting assignment by Président
AFFECTÉ_CHEF	Président	EN ATTENTE	Assigned to a Chef de service — not yet accepted
AFFECTÉ_AGENT	Chef de service	EN ATTENTE	Chef accepted and assigned to a specific Agent
EN_COURS	Agent	EN COURS	Agent actively intervening in the field
REFUSÉ_CHEF	Chef de service	EN ATTENTE	Chef refused → returned to Président with reason
REFUSÉ_AGENT	Agent	EN ATTENTE	Agent refused → returned to Chef de service with reason
RÉSOLU	Agent	TERMINÉ	Problem resolved — mandatory proof photo uploaded
CLÔTURÉ	Citoyen / System	TERMINÉ	Rated by Citoyen or auto-closed after 7 days

5.3 Service Rating
After transitioning to RÉSOLU status, the Citoyen receives a service rating invitation:
•	Rating from 1 to 5 stars (mandatory to validate the rating)
•	Optional free-text comment
•	Rating is optional — automatic closure after 7 days without rating
•	One rating per request (UNIQUE constraint in the database)

5.4 Happy Path Scenario
1.	A Citoyen from Sousse Jawhara reports a nid-de-poule on rue Ibn Khaldoun. They can use the chatbot for guidance.
2.	GPS automatically locates the incident. The Citoyen receives an in-app confirmation.
3.	The Président assigns the request to the Chef du département Voirie.
4.	The Chef accepts and assigns to a field Agent.
5.	The Agent intervenes, uploads a before/after photo, marks RÉSOLU.
6.	The Citoyen receives a notification, sees the map pin turn green.
7.	The Citoyen rates the service: 4 stars + 'Réparation rapide, merci!'
 
6. Data Model (Database Schema)
PostgreSQL schema — 13 main tables. All tables include tenant_id for multi-tenant support.

6.1 Table Overview
Table	Role	Key Relations
delegations	Top-level administrative division	1 délégation → N municipalities, N users, N declarations
municipalities	Cities within délégations	N→1 délégation ; 1 municipality → N users, N teams
departments	Municipal départements (replaces services)	1 département → 1 chef, N agents, N categories (via dept_categories)
categories	Problem types (trilingual)	N:N with departments via dept_categories ; N→1 in declarations
dept_categories	Join table Category ↔ Département	FK to departments + categories ; composite UNIQUE key
users	All users (citoyen, agent, chef, président)	Role ENUM ; FK to delegation, municipality, team ; soft delete
teams	Field teams per département	N→1 municipality, N→1 department ; leader_id FK to users
declarations	Citizen signalements (central entity)	FK to category, citizen, delegation, municipality ; GIST index on coordinates
assignments	Assignments: Président→Chef→Agent	FK to declarations, users (assigned_by, assigned_to_chef, assigned_to_agent)
status_history	Immutable audit log of all status changes	INSERT only ; FK to declarations, users ; index on declaration_id
attachments	Photos and files linked to declarations	FK to declarations, users ; type ENUM (photo, pdf, preuve)
ratings	Citizen ratings (1-5 stars + optional comment)	UNIQUE(declaration_id) ; FK to declarations, users
notifications	In-app alerts for all users	FK to users ; reference_id nullable (generic UUID)
proposals	Municipal proposals for citizen voting	FK to users (published_by=Président) ; N:N via proposal_votes
proposal_votes	Approve/reject votes on proposals	UNIQUE(proposal_id, citizen_id) ; vote ENUM

6.2 Detailed SQL Schema
Table: departments (new — replaces services)
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
id	UUID	PK DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
name_fr	TEXT	NOT NULL — French department name
name_ar	TEXT	NOT NULL — Arabic name
name_en	TEXT	NOT NULL — English name
description	TEXT	NULLABLE
chef_id	UUID	FK → users(id) ; 1 chef per département
is_active	BOOLEAN	DEFAULT true — soft delete
tenant_id	UUID	NOT NULL — mandatory multi-tenant
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()
updated_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()

Table: dept_categories (new — N:N Category ↔ Département)
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
department_id	UUID	FK → departments(id) ; part of composite PK
category_id	UUID	FK → categories(id) ; part of composite PK
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()

PRIMARY KEY (department_id, category_id) — prevents duplicates. One category can belong to multiple départements.

Table: users (updated — role ENUM)
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
id	UUID	PK DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
email	TEXT	UNIQUE NOT NULL
password_hash	TEXT	NOT NULL — bcrypt cost ≥ 10
role	ENUM	citoyen | agent | chef_service | president
first_name	TEXT	NOT NULL
last_name	TEXT	NOT NULL
phone	TEXT	NULLABLE
delegation_id	UUID	FK → delegations(id) ; NULLABLE
municipality_id	UUID	FK → municipalities(id) ; NULLABLE
department_id	UUID	FK → departments(id) — for agents and chefs ; NULLABLE
team_id	UUID	FK → teams(id) ; NULLABLE
lang_pref	ENUM	fr | ar | en  DEFAULT 'fr'
is_active	BOOLEAN	DEFAULT true — mandatory soft delete
refresh_token	TEXT	NULLABLE
tenant_id	UUID	NOT NULL
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()
updated_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()

Table: declarations (central entity)
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
id	UUID	PK DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
ref_citoyen	TEXT	Auto-generated by trigger on INSERT — format: {DELEGATION}-DD-MM-YY-XXXX
ref_service	TEXT	Set by backend when Président assigns — format: {SERVICE}-DD-MM-YY-XXXX
title	TEXT	NOT NULL — max 100 characters
description	TEXT	NULLABLE — max 1000 characters
category_id	UUID	FK → categories(id)
citizen_id	UUID	FK → users(id) ; role=citoyen
internal_status	ENUM	SOUMIS | AFFECTÉ_CHEF | AFFECTÉ_AGENT | EN_COURS | REFUSÉ_CHEF | REFUSÉ_AGENT | RÉSOLU | CLÔTURÉ
citizen_status	ENUM	EN_ATTENTE | EN_COURS | TERMINÉ — computed from internal_status
priority	ENUM	faible | moyen | élevé | urgent  DEFAULT 'moyen'
priority_score	FLOAT	DEFAULT 0 — computed: votes×3 + age_days×0.5
latitude	FLOAT8	NULLABLE
longitude	FLOAT8	NULLABLE
address	TEXT	NULLABLE
delegation_id	UUID	FK → delegations(id)
municipality_id	UUID	FK → municipalities(id)
department_id	UUID	FK → departments(id) — set at assignment
votes_count	INTEGER	DEFAULT 0
is_deleted	BOOLEAN	DEFAULT false — soft delete
tenant_id	UUID	NOT NULL
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()
updated_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()

Table: assignments
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
id	UUID	PK DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
declaration_id	UUID	FK → declarations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
assigned_by	UUID	FK → users(id) — who created the assignment
assigned_to_chef	UUID	FK → users(id) ; NULLABLE — Chef de service assigned
assigned_to_agent	UUID	FK → users(id) ; NULLABLE — Agent assigned
notes	TEXT	NULLABLE — optional internal notes
is_active	BOOLEAN	DEFAULT true
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()
updated_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now() — auto via trigger

Table: status_history (immutable audit log)
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
id	UUID	PK DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
declaration_id	UUID	FK → declarations(id) ; indexed
old_status	ENUM	Previous internal_status value
new_status	ENUM	New internal_status value
changed_by	UUID	FK → users(id) — who triggered the change
raison	TEXT	NULLABLE — mandatory when status = REFUSÉ_CHEF or REFUSÉ_AGENT
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now() — INSERT ONLY, never updated

Table: ratings (updated — optional comment)
Column	Type	Constraints & Description
id	UUID	PK
declaration_id	UUID	FK → declarations(id) ; UNIQUE — 1 rating per request
citizen_id	UUID	FK → users(id)
score	SMALLINT	CHECK score ≥ 1 AND score ≤ 5 ; NOT NULL
comment	TEXT	NULLABLE — optional citizen comment
created_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	DEFAULT now()

Database Views
View	Purpose	Used By
v_declarations_citizen	Maps internal_status → citizen_status (3 states). Hides all internal flow.	GET /api/declarations/mine
v_map_declarations	Returns lat, lng, title, category, citizen_status, pin_color for all active declarations.	GET /api/declarations/map
 
7. Technical Architecture
7.1 Architecture Overview
FixMaCity follows a classic three-tier architecture: React frontend, Node.js/Express backend, PostgreSQL database. All communication between frontend and backend goes through a REST API secured by JWT.

Layer	Technology	Role
Frontend	React 18 + Vite	Single Page Application — 4 role-based interfaces + citizen map
Backend	Node.js + Express	REST API — business logic, auth, RBAC, Gemini proxy
Database	PostgreSQL + PostGIS	Relational data + geospatial queries (ST_DWithin)
File Storage	Cloudinary	Proof photos and attachments — never stored on server filesystem
AI Chatbot	Gemini API (server-side)	Trilingual citizen assistant — API key never exposed to client
Authentication	JWT + bcrypt	Signed JWT (HS256) in HTTP-only cookie
Maps	Leaflet.js or Mapbox GL	Interactive map with colored declaration pins

7.2 Backend Folder Structure
fixmacity-backend/
├── src/
│   ├── config/        # db.js (Supabase client), env validation
│   ├── middleware/    # auth.js, rbac.js, rateLimit.js
│   ├── routes/        # auth, citoyen, agent, chef, president, chatbot, map
│   ├── controllers/   # one controller per route file
│   ├── services/      # business logic (statusHistory, refGenerator, gemini)
│   └── app.js         # Express setup, CORS, Helmet, routes
├── .env
└── server.js

7.3 Reference ID Format
Every declaration receives two auto-generated reference IDs at different stages of its lifecycle:

When	Who	Format	Example
On citizen submission	DB trigger (auto on INSERT)	  {DELEGATION}-DD-MM-YY-XXXX  	SV-31-03-26-0001
When Président assigns	Backend generates	  {SERVICE}-DD-MM-YY-XXXX  	VR-31-03-26-0001

Délégation Code	Délégation Name
SV	Sousse Ville
SJ	Sousse Jawhara
SA	Sousse Sidi Abdelhamid

Service Code	Département
VR	Voirie & Routes
EP	Éclairage public
PD	Propreté & Déchets
EV	Espaces verts
EA	Réseaux & Drainage
ST	Signalisation routière
BP	Administratif
SG	Suggestions
 
8. API Endpoints
All routes prefixed with /api. Authentication via Bearer token in Authorization header. RBAC middleware enforced on every protected route.

8.1 Authentication — /api/auth
Method	Route	Role	Action
POST	/api/auth/register	Public	Register as Citoyen — role=citoyen assigned automatically
POST	/api/auth/login	Public	Login — returns JWT + user profile
GET	/api/auth/me	Auth (any)	Returns current authenticated user profile
POST	/api/auth/logout	Auth (any)	Invalidates session / refresh token

8.2 Declarations — /api/declarations
Method	Route	Role	Action
POST	/api/declarations	citoyen	Submit new signalement — triggers ref_citoyen auto-generation
GET	/api/declarations/mine	citoyen	List my own declarations (uses v_declarations_citizen view)
GET	/api/declarations/map	citoyen	All active declarations for map view (uses v_map_declarations view)
PUT	/api/declarations/:id	citoyen	Edit — ONLY if internal_status = SOUMIS
DELETE	/api/declarations/:id	citoyen	Soft delete (is_deleted=true) — ONLY if internal_status = SOUMIS
POST	/api/declarations/:id/vote	citoyen	Vote — one vote per Citoyen per declaration (UNIQUE enforced)
POST	/api/declarations/:id/rate	citoyen	Rate 1–5 stars + optional comment — only after RÉSOLU

8.3 Président — /api/president
Method	Route	Action
GET	/api/president/declarations	All incoming declarations — all délégations and all départements
POST	/api/president/declarations/:id/assign	Assign to Chef de service + generate ref_service
POST	/api/president/declarations/:id/reassign	Reassign refused declarations to a different Chef
GET	/api/president/users	List all staff (agents + chefs)
POST	/api/president/users	Create Agent or Chef de service account
PATCH	/api/president/users/:id	Update role / département / active status
DELETE	/api/president/users/:id	Soft deactivate (is_active = false)
GET	/api/president/departments	List all 8 départements with stats
POST	/api/president/propositions	Publish municipal proposal for citizen voting
GET	/api/president/dashboard	Platform-wide KPIs — all délégations
GET	/api/president/export	Export performance report (CSV or PDF)

8.4 Chef de service — /api/chef
Method	Route	Action
GET	/api/chef/declarations	All declarations assigned to my département
POST	/api/chef/declarations/:id/accept	Accept + assign to specific Agent
POST	/api/chef/declarations/:id/refuse	Refuse with mandatory written reason (body.reason required)
GET	/api/chef/agents	List my team agents with active request count
PATCH	/api/chef/agents/:id/deactivate	Soft deactivate agent (is_active = false)
GET	/api/chef/dashboard	Département statistics and KPIs
GET	/api/chef/export	Export département data as CSV

8.5 Agent — /api/agent
Method	Route	Action
GET	/api/agent/declarations	All declarations in my département/team
POST	/api/agent/declarations/:id/accept	Accept personally — internal_status → EN_COURS
POST	/api/agent/declarations/:id/refuse	Refuse with mandatory reason — returns to Chef de service
POST	/api/agent/declarations/:id/photo	Upload proof photo (JPG/PNG, max 10 MB via Cloudinary)
POST	/api/agent/declarations/:id/resolve	Mark RÉSOLU — HTTP 403 if no proof photo uploaded
GET	/api/agent/declarations/:id/comments	View internal comments on this declaration
POST	/api/agent/declarations/:id/comments	Add internal comment (visible to team + Chef only)

Agent cannot resolve a declaration without uploading at least one proof photo. The backend checks COUNT of proof photos before allowing the status change to RÉSOLU.

8.6 Chatbot — /api/chatbot
Method	Route	Role	Action
POST	/api/chatbot/message	citoyen (auth)	Send message → Gemini API called server-side. Rate limit: 20 req/min per user.

8.7 Business Logic Rules — Enforced in Backend
Rule	Enforcement	HTTP Error
Proof photo required to resolve	Check COUNT(proof_photos) > 0 before RÉSOLU	403 Forbidden
Refuse requires reason	body.reason must be non-empty string	400 Bad Request
Edit/delete only when SOUMIS	Check internal_status before allowing mutation	403 Forbidden
Vote uniqueness	UNIQUE constraint in DB + app check	409 Conflict
One rating per declaration	UNIQUE constraint on declaration_id in ratings	409 Conflict
Département isolation	Filter all queries by req.user.department_id	—
Log every status change	Insert to status_history after every transition	—
Citizen never sees internal status	Always map via v_declarations_citizen	—
Staff accounts by Président only	RBAC: POST /api/president/users only	403 Forbidden
Auto-close after 7 days	Scheduled job: RÉSOLU → CLÔTURÉ after 7 days no rating	—
 
9. Non-Functional Requirements
9.1 Performance
Indicator	Target	Method
Citizen initial page load	< 3 seconds	4G mobile connection (Tunisian network)
Sousse map with pins loading	< 4 seconds	Up to 500 active pins
Status update (polling)	< 30 seconds	HTTP polling every 30s in MVP
5 MB photo upload	< 8 seconds	4G · client-side compression · auto-retry
Geospatial duplicate search	< 1 second	ST_DWithin PostgreSQL with GIST index
Chatbot AI response (1st token)	< 3 seconds	LLM API call with streaming enabled
Platform availability	99.5% uptime	Measured over 30 days

9.2 Security
•	Authentication: JWT signed (HS256) stored in HTTP-only, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookie
•	Passwords: hashed with bcrypt (cost factor ≥ 10) — never stored in plain text
•	Strict RBAC: every API route checks role via middleware (req.user.role)
•	File uploads: stored on Cloudinary — never on the server filesystem
•	Rate limiting: 10 req/min on /api/auth/login and /api/auth/register · 20 req/min on /api/chatbot
•	Validation & sanitization: all inputs validated with express-validator server-side
•	Chatbot security: LLM API calls exclusively server-side Node.js. API key in .env only
•	HTTPS mandatory in production (TLS 1.2+). HTTP redirected to HTTPS
•	Security headers: helmet.js (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, etc.)

9.3 Multilingual & RTL
•	3 citizen languages: Arabic (AR) · French (FR) · English (EN)
•	Staff interfaces (Agent, Chef de service, Président): French only
•	Arabic requires full RTL layout — use CSS logical properties and dir='rtl' on <html>
•	Recommended library: i18next + react-i18next
•	Department names stored trilingually in DB (name_fr, name_ar, name_en)
•	The Chatbot detects the active session language and responds accordingly
 
10. Out of Scope — MVP v2.0
Feature	Reason Excluded	Target Version
In-app messaging (all roles)	Removed in v1.2. Automated notifications cover communication needs.	Permanently removed
SMS notifications	Requires Tunisian carrier integration + per-SMS cost + commercial agreement.	v1.5
Public map without login	Authentication required to access the map. Connected map encourages registration.	v2.0
Geographic heat map	Nice-to-have, not in the main flow. Useful for Président but not blocking.	v1.5
PDF export	Static reporting, not a priority. CSV covers MVP needs.	v1.5
WebSocket real-time	30s polling sufficient for MVP. WebSocket complexity not justified at launch.	v1.5
Native mobile app (iOS/Android)	Responsive mobile-first web sufficient for MVP.	v2.0
Online payments	Final and irrevocable decision: FixMaCity is a fully free public service.	Never
Mandatory text comment in rating	MVP rating is limited to stars + optional comment.	v1.5
 
11. Change Summary v1.2 → v2.0
#	Element	v1.2 (Previous)	v2.0 (Current)
1	Role terminology	Manager → Admin → Président	Chef de service · Président municipal
2	Services → Départements	'services' table — 1:N relation with categories	'departments' table + 'dept_categories' join table — N:N relation
3	Categories	1 category → 1 département only	1 category can belong to N départements
4	Citizen statuses	8 statuses visible including internal steps	3 simplified statuses: EN ATTENTE · EN COURS · TERMINÉ
5	Refusal → citizen status	Citoyen saw REFUSÉ	Citoyen stays on EN ATTENTE — refusal invisible
6	Service rating	Stars only (1-5)	Stars (1-5) + optional comment
7	In-app messaging	Removed in v1.2	Confirmed removed — notifications only
8	SMS notifications	Out of scope v1.2	Confirmed out of scope — email + in-app only
9	Municipal scope	Multi-tenant architecture	1 municipality (Sousse) · 3 délégations · 1 single Président

